 ## Errors
 
 The current routes usually return a flat JSON error such as `{"error":"..."}` and may include `details`. The client also accepts a nested error envelope for compatibility. A non-JSON response is treated as a server error.
+
+### Verification timestamp representation
+
+`verifiedAt` accepts a timezone-qualified ISO 8601 timestamp or a Unix millisecond integer; GET returns Unix milliseconds (or null when unknown). CLI 2.5.1 accepts equivalent ISO and millisecond readback values. It does not skip missing fields or permit mismatched verification times.
